      "content": "Indeed, sediment buildup can cause popping or knocking noises in water heaters as water and sediment bubbles or shifts with temperature changes. However, if the sounds occur at random times and you haven't recently noticed any changes in water pressure or appearance, it might be difficult to be certain. An air pocket phenomenon can cause fluctuations, but it's less common. To avoid the stress of guessing, still, the safest course of action is to consult a professional. They can accurately diagnose the problem without risking further issues or your safety.",
